issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in:\nv4.7.rc1.official [a4f5e8cdd]\nv4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc1 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - GeForce GTX 550 Ti - Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-2100 CPU @ 3.10GHz (4 threads) - 11.95 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe viewport UI for draggable points, update their position when the mouse pointer is moved over the viewport, after making a change in the inspector.\nExample nodes:\nLine2D\nPolygon2D\nRayCast2D\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- open the project: [viewport-ui-updates-on-mouse-over-viewport.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28804010/viewport-ui-updates-on-mouse-over-viewport.zip)\n- in the scene panel, select: Line2D\n- in the inspector, on the Points property, click on: PackedVector2Array\n  to unfold the positions of each point\n- change the y position of the second point (labeled 1) from: 100 to: 50\n\n### Issue\nThe viewport UI for the draggable second point doesn't update, until the mouse pointer is moved over the viewport.\n\nThe same thing happens with a Polygon2D's array position and a RayCast2D's target position.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebac456c-0007-40db-a498-055b64c80dd8\n\n### Expected\nUpdate the viewport UI for the draggable point when the inspector value changes.\nLike it does for the second point on the line behind the draggable point.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[viewport-ui-updates-on-mouse-over-viewport.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28804010/viewport-ui-updates-on-mouse-over-viewport.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","ava